# A tag arm narrows the matched element to its family's row (Claude's call under ruling
# OP, 13 November; the library's `@HostRole`, which bundles a seat element at its role):
# in the `Count.Ask` arm, `element`, an `Element (Count.* | rest) o`, is an
# `Element Count.* o`, so `@Answer` takes it.
# Written by Claude on the claude-self-hosting branch; subject to change.
module Narrow
emit r | Count.*

family Count

tag Count.Ask of Element Nat:
    by: Nat

@Answer: fn Element Count.* o -> @o
fn @Answer element = match element:
    Count.Ask(by=by): @ by

@HostOne: fn Element (Count.* | rest) o -> @o emit rest
fn @HostOne element = match element:
    Count.Ask(..): @Answer element
    otherwise: @Element element
